WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:06.410
There is an absolutely fascinating and chaotic
war that has developed between Donald Trump

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.529
and the Republican Party.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:13.440
It has the makings of exactly the type of
chaos that could endanger both Donald Trump's

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.230
political future and also the viability of
the Republican Party in the 2022 election

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.230
cycle.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.820
And not surprisingly, this is all about money.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.810
Back at his CPAC speech a couple of weeks
back, Donald Trump announced that he was not

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.170
yet announcing whether he would run in 2024.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:35.690
He said, we'll see how it goes, but that for
now, donate to him at Donald Trump dotcom.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.140
So that threw his Save America PAC.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.690
He can support the right Republican candidates
in 2022.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.500
And he also went on a very long rant slamming
certain Republicans.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.500
Remember this.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:54.650
Democrats don't have grandstanders like Mitt
Romney, little Ben Sasse, Richard Burr, Bill

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:04.260
Cassidy, Susan Collins, Lisa Murkowski, Pat
Toomey.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:15.979
And in the House, Tom Rice, South Carolina,
Adam Kinzinger, Dan Newhouse, Anthony Gonzalez,

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:17.880
that's another beauty.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:27.070
Fred Upton, Jami Herrera Butler, Peter Meyer,
John Katka, David Valadao and of course, the

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:33.860
war monger, a person that loves seeing our
troops fighting Liz Cheney.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.020
How about that?

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.180
So what is this all about?

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:43.180
Quite simply, this is about Trump wanting
to control the Republican Party and to be

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.729
kingmaker, Trump doesn't yet know whether
he will run in 2024 because it's not clear

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:52.280
what his position in the Republican Party
is going to be at that time.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.920
That's almost four years away.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.729
For now, most voters in the Republican Party
still support Donald Trump, but many Republican

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:01.480
elected officials don't.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:08.509
And Trump's best path to 2024 is to be a kingmaker
successfully in twenty twenty two.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.459
In order to do that, he needs to control the
donor money of the Republican Party.

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:19.340
And this has set up a major propaganda and
legal battle between Donald Trump and the

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.999
Republican Party, which is just exploding.

00:02:21.999 --> 00:02:28.180
The Republican Party says it has the right
period to use Trump's name and likeness for

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.730
fundraising purposes.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:35.249
Donald Trump has sent the Republican Party
a cease and desist letter saying, stop using

00:02:35.249 --> 00:02:41.180
my name, stop using my likeness to raise money
for the Republican Party.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:46.189
Trump wants to raise the money himself for
his PAC and then decide who to support in

00:02:46.189 --> 00:02:50.989
2022 and which Republicans to try to primary
and remove in 2022.

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:56.330
And he doesn't want to be competing with his
own name and image used by the Republican

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.989
Party to raise money, maybe as he would see
it, to support the wrong Republicans.

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:05.919
He doesn't want his name being used to raise
money by the GOP to then support the reelection

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:09.840
of Liz Cheney, for example, or Mitt Romney,
for example.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.749
So the legal battle is going to continue.

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:13.159
I don't know how that will go.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:19.059
I mean, it's a does the Republican Party have
a right to monetize a former president's name

00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:20.059
and likeness?

00:03:20.059 --> 00:03:21.059
I don't know the answer to that.

00:03:21.059 --> 00:03:22.299
That's a legal question.

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:27.510
But in the meantime, Donald Trump has released
a wild attack letter, the likes of which we've

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:32.239
never seen ever from a former president against
their own party.

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:38.549
Writing yesterday in a statement by Donald
Trump, No more money for rhinos.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:41.549
RINO means Republican in name only.

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:45.730
They do nothing but hurt the Republican Party
and our great voting base.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.549
They will never lead us to greatness.

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:53.540
Send your donation to Save America PAC at
Donald Trump Dotcom.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.699
We will bring it all back stronger than ever
before.

00:03:57.699 --> 00:04:04.309
A former Republican president is saying Do
not donate to my party to the Republican Party.

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:11.579
Donate to me instead of former president sending
a cease and desist letter to their own party

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:15.510
saying, don't mention me in trying to raise
money.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:21.099
And so this is unprecedented, of course, but
it's a grift on a few different layers.

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:25.271
First of all, Trump wants to control the money
because that's Trump's whole life, control

00:04:25.271 --> 00:04:26.940
the money, not someone else.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.990
That that's been Trump's entire career.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:34.189
Number two, Republican voters are willing
to donate some amount of money each election

00:04:34.189 --> 00:04:35.189
cycle.

00:04:35.189 --> 00:04:40.660
Trump wants it to go to him rather than to
someone else so that he can play kingmaker.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.979
Secondly, Trump can't tolerate any dissent.

00:04:44.979 --> 00:04:50.659
So he has this list of enemy Republicans,
rhinos, who he might even try to get primary

00:04:50.659 --> 00:04:54.099
challengers against for 2022.

00:04:54.099 --> 00:04:55.330
And he wants to control that.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.800
That's another reason why he says donate to
him, not to the Republican Party.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.569
And third, he wants to keep his options open
for 2024.

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:07.090
And in order to do that, him controlling the
Republican Party in 2022 is the natural and

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.129
most obvious path.

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:14.500
Now, there's maybe a fourth, which is Trump
maybe can use some of this money of either

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:20.330
towards campaign debt or keep it if he does
eventually run in twenty, twenty four instead

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.320
of using it in twenty twenty two.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.080
That really depends on the specifics of how
this PAC is set up.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.810
I emailed a couple of lawyers this morning
asking whether this is possibly what Trump

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.070
is also doing.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.200
Haven't heard back yet, so we'll look into
that more.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.979
But that's potentially the fourth layer of
the grift.

00:05:35.979 --> 00:05:37.719
And that's what Trump did with his fundraising.

00:05:37.719 --> 00:05:43.110
I think it was 70 something million after
the November twenty twenty election saying

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:49.250
give me money to try to overturn the election
results and fund recounts in Georgia and all

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.250
this stuff.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.099
He kept most of the money for his own campaign
debt.

00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:55.850
So that's the latest with Trump Trump in the
Republican Party.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.530
Now they're officially at war.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:02.219
This is Trump declared war against a certain
slate of Republicans at his CPAC speech two

00:06:02.219 --> 00:06:03.740
weeks ago.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:09.340
And now Donald Trump declaring legal war against
the Republican Party, sending a cease and

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.060
desist letter

